From: LuneOS <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gstreamer: rank camera pixel formats instead of opening in
 greyscale

QPlatformCamera::findBestCameraFormat() picks a format by comparing a tuple:

    isValid, sufficientFrameRate, width * height, pixelFormatScore, maxFrameRate

Three of those are degenerate for a libcamera device. libcamerasrc reports a
maxFrameRate of 0 for every format, which flattens the 2nd and 5th members;
every format of a given sensor reaches the same maximum resolution, which
flattens the 3rd. The 4th comes from cameraPixelFormatScore(), a virtual that
the base class answers with 0 and which only the Darwin backend overrides, so
it is flat too.

Every candidate therefore compares equal, ranges::max() returns the first
element, and libcamera enumerates greyscale first. The result is that a colour
camera opens in greyscale on the GStreamer backend, and an application has to
notice and re-assign QCamera::cameraFormat afterwards. That correction is not
free: it tears the camera down and rebuilds it a second time. On a PinePhone
Pro, switching sensors then reconfigures three times in 1.5 seconds -

    configuring streams: (0) 3264x2448-R8/Rec709
    configuring streams: (0) 4208x3120-R8/Rec709
    configuring streams: (0) 1280x720-YUV420/Rec709

- and the pipeline does not survive it.

Implement the scoring hook for GStreamer so a colour format is chosen up front
and the second reconfiguration never happens. Monochrome layouts rank lowest,
above only Format_Invalid, so a genuinely monochrome sensor still works.
Packed YUV ranks below planar: it maps to a DRM fourcc whose EGL image must be
sampled with samplerExternalOES while the dmabuf import binds a plain
sampler2D, so it renders incorrectly wherever camera buffers arrive as dmabuf.
JPEG ranks below raw colour as it costs a decoder hop.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff -ruN sc_a/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/mediacapture/qgstreamercamera.cpp sc_b/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/mediacapture/qgstreamercamera.cpp
--- a/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/mediacapture/qgstreamercamera.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/mediacapture/qgstreamercamera.cpp
@@ -188,6 +188,48 @@
     return true;
 }
 
+int QGstreamerCamera::cameraPixelFormatScore(QVideoFrameFormat::PixelFormat format,
+                                             QVideoFrameFormat::ColorRange) const
+{
+    /*
+     * findBestCameraFormat() ranks formats on a tuple whose other members are
+     * frequently degenerate: libcamerasrc reports a maxFrameRate of 0 for every
+     * format, and every format of a given sensor reaches the same maximum
+     * resolution. With the base implementation returning 0 for everything, all
+     * criteria tie, std::max returns the first element, and libcamera
+     * enumerates greyscale first - so a colour camera opens in greyscale.
+     *
+     * Rank what the pipeline can actually present instead.
+     */
+    switch (format) {
+    case QVideoFrameFormat::Format_Invalid:
+        return 0;
+
+    case QVideoFrameFormat::Format_Y8:
+    case QVideoFrameFormat::Format_Y16:
+        /* Monochrome: correct only for a genuinely monochrome sensor. */
+        return 1;
+
+    case QVideoFrameFormat::Format_YUYV:
+    case QVideoFrameFormat::Format_UYVY:
+        /*
+         * Packed YUV maps to a DRM fourcc whose EGL image has to be sampled
+         * with samplerExternalOES. The dmabuf import binds a plain sampler2D,
+         * so these render incorrectly wherever camera buffers arrive as
+         * dmabuf. Usable as a fallback, but never a first choice.
+         */
+        return 2;
+
+    case QVideoFrameFormat::Format_Jpeg:
+        /* Needs a decoder hop, and gives no control over the decoded layout. */
+        return 3;
+
+    default:
+        /* Planar and semi-planar YUV, and the RGB layouts. */
+        return 4;
+    }
+}
+
 void QGstreamerCamera::updateCameraProperties()
 {
 #if QT_CONFIG(linux_v4l)
diff -ruN sc_a/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/mediacapture/qgstreamercamera_p.h sc_b/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/mediacapture/qgstreamercamera_p.h
--- a/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/mediacapture/qgstreamercamera_p.h
+++ b/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/mediacapture/qgstreamercamera_p.h
@@ -78,6 +78,9 @@
 private:
     QGstreamerCamera(QCamera *camera);
 
+    int cameraPixelFormatScore(QVideoFrameFormat::PixelFormat format,
+                               QVideoFrameFormat::ColorRange colorRange) const override;
+
     void updateCameraProperties();
 
 #if QT_CONFIG(linux_v4l)
